From 97a58da81b5aeb9f1e32ef31910bf52a3762e90b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anthony Chinedu Echem <phexaraltd@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:17:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] Add clinical query understanding, tool routing, safety
 screen, supersession and faithfulness

* Query understanding normalises brand names and US spelling to UK generics
  and extracts age, weight, medicines and intents (knowledge/lexicon.yaml).
* Deterministic tool routing attaches verified regimen, local anaesthetic,
  adrenaline and medication safety cards to answers, streamed before the
  model writes, and never shows an adult dose for an unaged child.
* Medication safety screen combines the interaction table with patient
  medicine, allergy and condition rules (knowledge/safety_rules.yaml).
* Guideline supersession graph demotes and labels withdrawn guidance and
  marks it in the prompt (knowledge/supersession.yaml).
* Claim level lexical faithfulness on every answer plus an opt in LLM judge.
* Answerability gate abstains when the question's specific terms are absent
  from the evidence (offline abstention accuracy 0.90 to 1.00).
* Provider router with ordered fallbacks and circuit breakers; vendor SDK
  errors no longer surface as 500s.
* Shared Redis or in process LRU answer cache, HMAC keyed audit hashes,
  feedback capture and a governance summary endpoint.
* Constant time API key checks, Retry-After on 429, security headers,
  route level HTTP metrics, comma separated list settings fixed.
* Stronger extractive generator (fact recall 0.82 to 0.92).
