@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+# Security and data protection
+
+Report vulnerabilities privately to the maintainer rather than in a public issue.
+
+## Design summary
+
+* Identifiers (names with titles, valid NHS numbers, postcodes, dates of birth, phones, emails) are redacted
+  before text reaches retrieval, a model vendor, the cache, the audit log or a feedback record.
+* The audit log stores an HMAC of the redacted question keyed with `RC_AUDIT_SALT`, never the text.
+* API keys are compared in constant time; governance data needs a separate admin key.
+* Responses carry `nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer` and `Cache-Control:
+  no-store`; the interface is served with a restrictive Content Security Policy.
+* For organisations whose information governance forbids off site processing, set `RC_LLM_PROVIDER=ollama`
+  and `RC_LLM_FALLBACKS=` so no text leaves the network.
+
+## Before production
+
+Set a long random `RC_AUDIT_SALT`, real `RC_API_KEYS` and `RC_ADMIN_API_KEYS`, `RC_ENV=production`
+(which disables keyless development access), restrict `RC_CORS_ORIGINS`, and complete a DPIA.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0001-deterministic-tools-outside-the-prompt.md b/docs/adr/0001-deterministic-tools-outside-the-prompt.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1a35eb6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0001-deterministic-tools-outside-the-prompt.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# ADR 0001: Deterministic tool results stay outside the model prompt
+
+**Status:** accepted, version 2.
+
+Tool cards (regimens, local anaesthetic ceilings, adrenaline, safety screen) are streamed to the clinician as
+their own event and are not inserted into the model's context. If they were, the model could repeat a
+formulary figure that no cited source contains, and the figure check in the citation validator would either
+flag a correct number or have to be weakened. Keeping the two channels apart means every number in the
+narrative is still traceable to a cited passage, and every number in a card is traceable to a reviewed file.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0002-supersession-graph.md b/docs/adr/0002-supersession-graph.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6ebaaf2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-supersession-graph.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# ADR 0002: A hand curated supersession graph rather than date heuristics
+
+**Status:** accepted, version 2.
+
+Penalising old documents by age alone would demote long standing guidance that is still current (NICE CG19
+dates from 2004). Instead, rules in `backend/app/knowledge/supersession.yaml` name what replaced what, match on
+title, publisher, URL, source or year, are validated for cycles on load, and resolve chains to the newest
+edition. The cost is curation; the benefit is that only genuinely withdrawn advice is demoted, and the
+clinician is told what replaced it.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0003-provider-router.md b/docs/adr/0003-provider-router.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5276fb2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0003-provider-router.md
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# ADR 0003: Provider router with circuit breakers
+
+**Status:** accepted, version 2.
+
+Vendor SDKs raise their own exception types, which previously escaped as HTTP 500. The router treats any
+provider exception as a failure, falls through an ordered chain ending in the extractive generator, and opens
+a circuit after repeated failures so an outage costs one call, not every request. Streaming only falls back
+before the first token, so a clinician never reads an answer stitched from two models.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0004-answerability-gate.md b/docs/adr/0004-answerability-gate.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9e443ca
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0004-answerability-gate.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# ADR 0004: IDF weighted question coverage as an answerability gate
+
+**Status:** accepted, version 2.
+
+The top passage score alone let off topic questions through when they shared common words with the corpus
+(implant, dose). Coverage weights each informative question term by inverse document frequency, so the rare
+words that define the question dominate. Calibrated on the golden set, a threshold of 0.20 separates the
+unanswerable items (about 0.08) from the lowest answerable non emergency item (about 0.47). Emergencies bypass
+the gate.
